{"answer":"Your recent record does not show a high training volume: 3 device-detected sessions across 28 days, with no recorded sessions in the last 7 days. It therefore cannot show that recorded training is the reason for your exhaustion; unlogged exercise or physical work is still unknown. [e383ef8f-e1] [e383ef8f-e10]

You did report tiredness on several recent check-ins, and the last 7 days were 2.0 hours below your usual sleep; those observations line up with feeling run-down but do not establish why. [e383ef8f-e3] [e383ef8f-e11]

When did this begin, and what changed around then? How have you been sleeping and feeling on waking? Do you have any current pain? And has there been exercise or physically demanding work that was not recorded?","outcome":"clarification","reason":"Recorded training is low, but the cause of current exhaustion cannot be determined without timing, sleep/waking, pain, and unlogged-load information."}

{"answer":"This does not look like too much *recorded* training. The heavy house-moving work was unrecorded, and its timing lines up with the exhaustion, but it cannot establish the reason. [59970807-context] [e383ef8f-e1]

Treat that move as a substantial recent physical demand: take today as rest or only very easy movement, and do not add a hard workout until your waking energy is back to usual. You report no pain or other discomfort. [59970807-context]

